# Taste skills (project)

This project includes the Leonxlnx/taste-skill pack under `.cursor/skills/` and `.agents/skills/`.

When the user asks for landing-page design, portfolio UI, visual polish, anti-generic “AI slop” frontend work, redesign of marketing surfaces, brandkit, image-to-code, or a named style (minimalist, high-end, brutalist, stitch) — read and follow the matching skill before coding:

| Ask / vibe | Skill |
|---|---|
| Default anti-slop frontend / landing / portfolio | `design-taste-frontend` |
| Upgrade an existing UI without rewrite | `redesign-existing-projects` |
| Clean editorial minimal | `minimalist-ui` |
| Premium / Awwwards-tier | `high-end-visual-design` |
| Industrial brutalist | `industrial-brutalist-ui` |
| Brand tokens / kit | `brandkit` |
| Screenshot → code | `image-to-code` |
| Gen UI from image (web / mobile) | `imagegen-frontend-web` / `imagegen-frontend-mobile` |
| Stitch / GPT-oriented taste | `stitch-design-taste` / `gpt-taste` |
| Force complete UI output | `full-output-enforcement` |

Do **not** auto-apply these to normal dashboard/CRM bugfixes or backend work unless the user asks for a visual redesign. Prefer matching the existing Advanced Sales theme (Luxury / Light / Desert) when editing product UI inside the app.
